Output lilbee-fleet-drawer.gif
Output lilbee-fleet-drawer.mp4
Set Shell "bash"
Set FontSize 15
Set Width 1700
Set Height 950
Set Padding 20
Set TypingSpeed 55ms
Set Theme { "background": "#191724", "foreground": "#e0def4", "black": "#26233a", "red": "#eb6f92", "green": "#31748f", "yellow": "#f6c177", "blue": "#9ccfd8", "magenta": "#c4a7e7", "cyan": "#ebbcba", "white": "#e0def4", "brightBlack": "#6e6a86", "brightRed": "#eb6f92", "brightGreen": "#31748f", "brightYellow": "#f6c177", "brightBlue": "#9ccfd8", "brightMagenta": "#c4a7e7", "brightCyan": "#ebbcba", "brightWhite": "#e0def4", "cursor": "#e0def4", "selection": "#403d52" }
Hide
Type "lilbee-tui"
Enter
Sleep 5s
Type "Reply with just the word: ready."
Sleep 800ms
Enter
Sleep 120s
Show
Sleep 2s
Ctrl+g
Sleep 3s
Type "/rebuild"
Sleep 800ms
Enter
Sleep 1500ms
Enter
Sleep 32s
Type "How does lilbee split a large model across multiple GPUs?"
Sleep 1s
Enter
Sleep 40s
Sleep 2s
